WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.030
- I've been deep in these documents,

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.400
each of which is a piece

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.020
of evidence that helps me piece together

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.870
a very important question,
which is who got rich

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:15.169
off this 20 year bore that
we fought in Afghanistan?

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:17.075
(bombs exploding)

00:00:17.075 --> 00:00:18.183
(guns hosts)

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:19.016
(people screaming)

00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:19.849
But first, let me tell you what happened

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:21.890
on August 15th, 2021.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.490
The Taliban had entered Kabul after taking

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.140
over the entire country of Afghanistan.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.430
The war ended as it had begun

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.700
with the Taliban in power once again.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.060
You probably remember the scenes

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:35.848
from the Kabul airport,

00:00:35.848 --> 00:00:38.540
total chaos as Afghans
tried to flee their country.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.830
But there's one guy who
saw a business opportunity

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:42.830
in all of this.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:45.410
This guy, Eric Prince, generously offered

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:49.110
to help charter a plane to
evacuate people from Kabul,

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.190
the price tag, $6,500 per person.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.790
That was the market price
that Eric Prince decided.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.800
But this wasn't the first
time Eric Prince used

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.000
the war in Afghanistan to get rich.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.210
In fact, this was one of
the last of many instances

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.280
where this guy profited off the Afghan war

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.770
and some of the ways he did
it were kind of messed up.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.610
So after digging through
the numbers, the reports,

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.100
the Senate hearings, all of it,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.090
we've established a list
of some of the top people

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:23.090
who got crazy stupid rich
off of the war in Afghanistan

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.950
- On my orders, the United
States military has begun

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.010
strikes against Al-Qaeda
terrorist training camps

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.207
and military installations

00:01:31.207 --> 00:01:33.602
of the Taliban regime in Afghanistan.

00:01:33.602 --> 00:01:36.650
(disconcerting music)

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.200
- Before we get into our list

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.990
I want to talk about
an important term here

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.761
which is government contractor.

00:01:42.761 --> 00:01:44.570
- $300 hundred million
in government contracts.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.130
- U.S. defense contractor.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.500
- Our broken system of
government contractor.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.220
- [Narrator] At U.S. Federal
Contractor Registration,

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.340
we know that a government
contract is worth more

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.790
than the dollars awarded.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.210
- Here in the United States

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.228
we love the free market.

00:01:58.228 --> 00:01:59.520
(eerie music)

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.070
- I'm talking about this.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:03.710
- So instead of having the
clunky old federal government

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.630
take care of all things war,

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:09.200
we hire a lot of private
companies to do it for us.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.470
This is companies that make our weapons,

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:14.820
feed our soldiers, build
our bases, fuel our tanks

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.228
and literally fight our wars.

00:02:17.228 --> 00:02:18.651
(bomb explosion)

00:02:18.651 --> 00:02:20.984
(gun shots)

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:24.260
Yes, we have private armies

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.400
that we call security companies

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.930
that basically are soldiers for hire.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.820
What this allows the government to do is

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.410
post a job out there.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:36.050
Like we need someone to
build a road in Afghanistan.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.030
And in theory, what happens is a bunch

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.064
of private companies come
together and they all bid

00:02:40.064 --> 00:02:42.920
on how much it would
cost to build this road.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.850
And whatever company gives the best price

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.680
is chosen to go build that road.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.410
It's supposed to help the
government get the best price.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.050
Okay, so where am I going with this?

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.030
What I want you to
understand is that there

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.130
is this bidding process
for private companies

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.490
to go do things that the government needs,

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:02.600
but in war time a lot of
those processes of bidding

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.280
go out the window because
we're in war time.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.900
So it's like an emergency.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.230
So instead you get a lot

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.840
of situations where there
is no bidding on contracts.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.060
The government needs something done

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.500
in Afghanistan really quickly.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.710
This company could do it.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.060
Name your price.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.060
We'll give you whatever you need.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:18.893
- [Narrator] As a client,

00:03:18.893 --> 00:03:21.210
the U.S. government is guaranteed to have

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.260
the funds to pay you
and will always pay you.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.710
And it's that very process

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:28.860
that allowed people to take advantage

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.570
of a system to let billions
and billions of unaccounted

00:03:33.657 --> 00:03:35.380
for dollars be poured
into private companies.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.660
All of this contributed to what a former

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.514
Secretary of Defense call a culture

00:03:39.514 --> 00:03:42.570
of endless money inside the Pentagon.

